NNAAMMEE
     tsort - topological sort

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ttssoorrtt [_f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ttssoorrtt reads pairs of items from _f_i_l_e (or the standard input,
     if no _f_i_l_e is given) and prints, on the standard output, a
     sequence of all the items such that each item comes before
     every item that must follow it, according to the pairs
     given.

     The input consists of pairs of items (words) separated by
     blanks, tabs, or newlines.  A pair in which the two items
     are the same simply records that the item is present in the
     input set.  Otherwise, a pair means that the first item must
     precede the second in the output ordering.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     ssoorrtt

DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     ttssoorrtt reports and exits if its input holds an odd number of
     items, or if a word is longer than 99 characters.  If the
     given ordering contains a cycle, ttssoorrtt first dumps the items
     still involved in the cycle, in no particular order, then
     reports `tsort: cycles' and exits with a nonzero status.
